{% comment %}
  Cullinan: an accordion's own open/close arrow -- two bars that meet as a
  chevron at rest and rotate flat into a single line (a minus) once the
  <details> around them opens. See "The accordion arrow" in assets/crown.css
  for the shape and motion this was built against (moonmagic.com's own
  chevron, hestiahome.bg's own plus-to-minus motion), and the notes below
  for why each call site is shaped the way it is.

  Renders only the box and its two wings -- it carries no position or size of
  its own, because every site already has both for whatever icon used to sit
  there (Dawn's own `summary .icon-caret`, the footer's own, the metal menu's
  own, Контакти's own .contact-methods__toggle). The default output keeps the
  class "icon-caret" precisely so those rules keep applying unchanged; only
  Контакти needs `bare: true`, since its own toggle has never carried that
  class and must not start now (Dawn's generic `summary .icon-caret` rule
  would otherwise reach in and reposition it).

  Accepts:
  - bare: {Boolean, optional} true to leave the "icon-caret" class off the
    outer box, for a site whose own wrapper already positions and sizes it.
  - extra_class: {String, optional} classes to add alongside the default, e.g.
    a site's own existing toggle class.

  Usage:
    {% render 'icon-accordion-caret' %}
    {% render 'icon-accordion-caret', bare: true, extra_class: 'contact-methods__toggle' %}
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  assign outer_class = 'cj-caret'
  unless bare
    assign outer_class = outer_class | append: ' icon-caret'
  endunless
  if extra_class
    assign outer_class = outer_class | append: ' ' | append: extra_class
  endif
-%}
<span class="{{ outer_class }}" aria-hidden="true">
  <span class="cj-caret__wing cj-caret__wing--left"></span>
  <span class="cj-caret__wing cj-caret__wing--right"></span>
</span>
